 typical tax treatment for 1978, the question likely treats business expenses as deductions *from* gross income to get AGI. Let’s test:  \nAGI = Gross Income − Business Expenses (if deductible above-the-line), and Taxable Income = AGI − Exemptions − Itemized Deductions (here, non-business expenses may be itemized).  \nGiven: Taxable Income = $15,000, Exemptions = $1,500, Non-business Expenses = $3,000 (likely itemized deductions).  \nSo AGI − Exemptions − Non-business Expenses = Taxable Income ⇒ AGI − 1,500 − 3,000 = 15,000 ⇒ AGI = $19,500.  \nThen Gross Income = AGI + Business Expenses = $19,500 + $6,000 = $25,500.  \nThis matches option **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
