      "generated_answer": "The brother's cutting of the timber on the arable land—which is more valuable for cultivation than for timber—constitutes an improvement that benefits the property by converting it to a higher use. However, as a life tenant, the brother is not entitled to make changes that alter the character of the property without permission, even if the change increases value. This is an example of ameliorative waste because it involves a beneficial change made without consent that affects the inheritance rights of the remainderman.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
