    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The logistic growth model shows that population growth rate is maximal at half the carrying capacity (K/2), and the population stabilizes at K. To control a pest like mosquitoes effectively, reducing the environment's carrying capacity (e.g., by eliminating breeding sites) lowers K, thereby reducing the equilibrium population size. Maintaining the population at K/2 (option G) would actually maximize growth and increase numbers over time, which is counterproductive for control.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
