    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We analyze the equation $ x^{\\log y} = y^{\\log x} $. Taking logarithms on both sides and simplifying using log properties, we find that this equation holds for all $ x, y > 0 $ satisfying $ \\log y \\cdot \\log x = \\log x \\cdot \\log y $, which is always true. However, domain restrictions require $ x > 0 $ and $ y > 0 $, so the equation holds for all $ (x, y) $ in the open first quadrant.\n\nThus, the graph is **the open first quadrant**.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
