    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7462",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Can we use the method of compass and straightedge construction to construct the edge length of a cube, such that the volume of the cube is equal to X time the volume of a given cube, where X belongs to the set {{3,17,8,27,343,1331}}? Return the answer list for the respective values of X with 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0]\nB. [1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0]\nC. [0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1]\nD. [0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0]\nE. [0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1]\nF. [0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1]\nG. [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\nH. [1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1]\nI. [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]\nJ. [1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In compass and straightedge construction, we can only construct lengths that involve square roots and rational operations; cube roots are not constructible unless reducible. For a cube with volume $ X $ times a given cube, the side length must scale by $ \\sqrt[3]{X} $. The cube roots of $ X = 3, 17, 1331 $ are not constructible; $ \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2 $, $ \\sqrt[3]{27} = 3 $, $ \\sqrt[3]{343} = 7 $, and $ \\sqrt[3]{1} = 1 $ are rational, so only $ X = 8, 27, 343 $ are constructible, but $ X=1 $ is not in the list; checking values: $ \\sqrt[3]{8}, \\sqrt[3]{27}, \\sqrt[3]{343} $ are integers (constructible), while $ \\sqrt[3]{3}, \\sqrt[3]{17}, \\sqrt[3]{1331} = 11 $ — wait: $ 1331 = 11^3 $, so $ \\sqrt[3]{1331} = 11 $, also rational.\n\nThus, $ X = 8, 27, 343, 1331 $ all have rational cube roots (integers), so constructible; $ X=3,17 $ do not. So: [0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1] → C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 353,
        "output_tokens": 356,
        "total_tokens": 709
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
