    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) in an FM system is related to the input SNR and the modulation index β by the formula:  \n$$(SNR)_{out} \\approx (SNR)_{in} + 10 \\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{3}{2} \\beta^2\\right)$$  \nGiven $(SNR)_{in} = 40$ dB, we compute for each β:  \n- For β = 5: $10 \\log(3/2 \\times 25) \\approx 10 \\log(37.5) \\approx 15.7$ dB → 40 + 15.7 = 55.7 dB  \n- For β = 10: $10 \\log(3/2 \\times 100) = 10 \\log(150) \\approx 21.76$ dB → ~61.76 dB ≈ 61.7 dB  \n- For β = 105: $10 \\log(3/2 \\times 11025) = 10 \\log(16537.5) \\approx 42.185$ dB → ~82.185 dB  \nThis matches Option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
