    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To design the square key, we use the shaft radius $r = 1.5\\text{ in.}$ and the applied torque $T = 30,000\\text{ lb-in.}$, resulting in a tangential force $F = T/r = 20,000\\text{ lbs.}$ For a square key with width $w$ and length $L$, the shear stress is $\\tau = F/(wL) \\le 11,000\\text{ psi}$ and the bearing stress is $\\sigma = 2F/(wL) \\le 22,000\\text{ psi}$, both yielding the requirement $wL \\ge 1.818\\text{ in}^2$. Testing option A ($w=0.5, L=3$): $wL = 1.5 < 1.818$ (fails); testing option D ($w=0.75, L=2.5$): $wL = 1.875 > 1.818$ (passes).\n\n\\boxed{D}",
