    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the open-circuit EMF, use the formula $ E = 4.44 \\cdot f \\cdot \\phi \\cdot N \\cdot K_p \\cdot K_d $, where $ f = 60 $ Hz, $ \\phi = 0.025 $ Wb, $ N = 6 \\text{ poles} \\times 12 \\text{ slots/pole} \\times 4 \\text{ conductors/slot} / 2 = 144 $ turns (since 2 conductors = 1 turn), $ K_p = \\sin(5/6 \\cdot 90^\\circ) = \\sin(150^\\circ) = 0.966 $, and $ K_d = \\sin(30^\\circ / 2) / \\sin(30^\\circ / 2) = 1 $ (assuming full pitch for distribution, as not specified otherwise). Correcting: 144 turns * 1/3 (since Y-connected and 3 phases → 48 turns per phase), then $ E = 4.44 \\cdot 60 \\cdot 0.025 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 0.966 \\approx 308.5 $ V, closest to 296 V.  \nThe closest and most accurate option is A. 296 volts.  \nThus, $\\boxed{\\text{A}}$.",
