    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the open-circuit EMF of a 3-phase alternator, use the formula:  \n$ E = 4.44 \\cdot f \\cdot N \\cdot \\phi \\cdot K_p \\cdot K_d $,  \nwhere $ f = 60 $ Hz, total conductors per phase = $ \\frac{12 \\text{ slots/pole} \\times 6 \\text{ poles} \\times 4 \\text{ conductors/slot}}{3 \\text{ phases}} = 96 $, so $ N = 48 $ turns per phase; $ \\phi = 0.025 $ Wb; pitch factor $ K_p = \\sin(90^\\circ \\times \\frac{5}{6}) = \\sin(75^\\circ) \\approx 0.966 $; distribution factor $ K_d = \\frac{\\sin(m \\beta /2)}{m \\sin(\\beta/2)} $ with $ m = 12/6 = 2 $ slots/pole/phase and $ \\beta = 180^\\circ / 6 = 30^\\circ $, giving $ K_d \\approx 0.966 $.  \nThus, $ E_{\\text{phase}} = 4.44 \\times 60 \\times 48 \\times 0.025 \\times 0.966 \\times 0.966 \\approx 246.5 $ V; line voltage $ E_L = \\sqrt{3} \\times 246.5 \\approx 426 $ V.  \nThe closest option is **425 volts**, so the answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
