    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To achieve dynamic similarity in a gravity-dominated flow (sluice gate), we use the Froude number scaling, where the length scale ratio is $L_r = 1/20$. The model head $h_m$ is $H_p / 20 = 20 / 20 = 1$ meter. The discharge scale ratio is $Q_r = L_r^{2.5} = (1/20)^{2.5}$, so the prototype discharge $Q_p = Q_m / (1/20)^{2.5} = 0.5 \\times 20^{2.5} \\approx 0.5 \\times 1788.85 = 894.4$ m$^3/$s.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
