    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The study found that older individuals with higher financial assets were more likely to accept preventive home visits than those with lower assets, indicating a socioeconomic disparity in acceptance rates. Although the difference was somewhat reduced when considering municipal invitation procedures, the initial association shows a social imbalance. Therefore, the evidence supports the conclusion that acceptance rates are socially imbalanced.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
