    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The study found a strong positive correlation between corrected QT dispersion (QTcD) and left ventricular hypertrophy (LVH) in hypertensive patients, with high sensitivity and specificity at a cut-off of 60 ms. QTcD was significantly higher in hypertensive patients with LVH compared to those without, and it effectively distinguished those with LVH. Therefore, the evidence supports that QTcD can predict LVH in hypertensive patients.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
