      "generated_answer": "Norman’s socialist commune on Ventura Island failed because the leadership by Herman and Catherine Wolf imposed inefficient practices—such as a rigid nine-hour workday that incentivized laziness—and suppressed Norman’s initiative, including stealing his gold-finding device. Catherine Wolf further undermined the project by abandoning it, declaring family life too “capitalistic,” which eroded cohesion and morale. Ultimately, Norman had to appeal to external authority (his father and the Governor) to restore order and replace the Red Flag with the American one, confirming the incompatibility of the imposed socialist model with effective self-governance and productivity.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Norman’s socialist commune failed due to inefficient work practices, theft of his device by the Wolfes, and Catherine Wolf’s abandonment of the project, leading to low productivity and the need for external intervention to restore order.}}",
