    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Holmes refuses to let Watson examine him because he is feigning his illness to trick Culverton Smith into confessing. If Watson—a doctor—had examined him, he would have easily discovered the ruse. Therefore, Holmes had to maintain the charade of an infectious disease to keep Watson at a distance.\n\n\\boxed{Holmes excludes Watson from examining him to prevent his doctor friend from discovering that the illness is a ruse. By claiming the condition is highly infectious, he keeps Watson at a distance to ensure his plan to trap Culverton Smith succeeds.}",
