    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **J**. Garrison’s argument—that free Black people are citizens entitled to full constitutional rights—was directly contradicted by the *Dred Scott v. Sanford* (1857) decision, in which the Supreme Court ruled that Black people, whether free or enslaved, were not U.S. citizens and had no rights under the Constitution. This ruling explicitly rejected the very principle Garrison defended in his 1831 appeal.  \n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
