    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The excerpt justifies raising revenue through duties on trade in the American colonies, primarily to protect British commercial interests and pay for colonial defense. This aligns most closely with the use of protective tariffs during the Industrial Revolution, which also aimed to shield domestic industries and generate government revenue through import taxes. Both policies prioritized national economic advantage and revenue generation via trade regulation.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
