      "generated_answer": "The author argues that Western Europe’s “quantum jump” to global hegemony was enabled by exploiting the ecosystems and resources of other continents through conquest and ecological luck. The conquest of the Aztec Empire (Option E) exemplifies this by demonstrating how European powers seized vast resources, labor, and land in the Americas, fueling their economic and imperial rise. Other options either occurred later (like the Industrial Revolution) or were unrelated to European resource exploitation during 1450–1750.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
