      "generated_answer": "The Brown v. Board of Education decision addressed the unfulfilled promise of equal protection under the law, originally guaranteed by the 14th Amendment during Reconstruction, which aimed to secure civil rights for formerly enslaved people. Despite Reconstruction’s constitutional amendments, racial segregation in education persisted for decades, making Reconstruction the foundational initiative whose promises had not been realized. Thus, the correct answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
