      "generated_answer": "The law, passed in 1826, criminalized the forced or fraudulent removal of Black people from Pennsylvania with the intent to enslave them, indicating a protective stance by the state—despite Pennsylvania having abolished slavery渐进ly starting in 1780. This reflects the tension between Northern states like Pennsylvania, which had moved toward abolition (even if imperfectly), and Southern states and pro-slavery interests that sought to preserve and expand slavery, especially via fugitive slave disputes. While related to federal-state conflicts (Option E), the core tension here is explicitly regional and ideological over slavery’s continuation.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
